{
  "name": "nxwright-language",
  "displayName": "nxwright",
  "description": "Design, write, simulate, and test Nextion screen apps in VS Code.",
  "version": "0.2.0",
  "publisher": "nxwright",
  "icon": "images/icon.png",
  "license": "Apache-2.0",
  "repository": {
    "type": "git",
    "url": "https://github.com/nixiewright/nxwright",
    "directory": "editors/vscode"
  },
  "homepage": "https://github.com/nixiewright/nxwright",
  "bugs": {
    "url": "https://github.com/nixiewright/nxwright/issues"
  },
  "private": true,
  "engines": {
    "vscode": "^1.82.0"
  },
  "categories": [
    "Programming Languages"
  ],
  "main": "./out/extension.js",
  "activationEvents": [
    "workspaceContains:**/app.toml"
  ],
  "contributes": {
    "languages": [
      {
        "id": "nxwright",
        "aliases": [
          "nxwright"
        ],
        "extensions": [
          ".nx"
        ],
        "configuration": "./language-configuration.json"
      }
    ],
    "grammars": [
      {
        "language": "nxwright",
        "scopeName": "source.nxwright",
        "path": "./syntaxes/nxwright.tmLanguage.json"
      }
    ],
    "configuration": [
      {
        "title": "General",
        "properties": {
          "nxwright.command": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "default": [],
            "markdownDescription": "The command that runs nxwright: the program, then its first arguments. When it is empty, the default, the extension runs the `nxwright` command that `pip install` gives, if it is on PATH; else `python -P -m nxwright` with the first Python that runs it: the interpreter chosen in VS Code, when the Python extension is installed, then `python3`, `python`, and on Windows `py -3`. From a copy of nxwright's repository, use for example `[\"python\", \"${workspaceFolder}/nxwright/run.py\"]`; `${workspaceFolder}` stands for the workspace's first folder."
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "title": "Page preview",
        "properties": {
          "nxwright.previewGrid": {
            "type": "integer",
            "default": 1,
            "minimum": 1,
            "markdownDescription": "The grid, in pixels, that a component's edges snap to when dragged in the page preview. 1 for none."
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "title": "Simulator",
        "properties": {
          "nxwright.simulator.serialPort": {
            "type": "string",
            "default": "",
            "markdownDescription": "The serial port a simulation's serial line is connected to, such as `COM4`, when its launch configuration gives no `serialPort`. Empty for none."
          },
          "nxwright.simulator.serialBaud": {
            "type": "integer",
            "default": 9600,
            "enum": [
              2400,
              4800,
              9600,
              19200,
              31250,
              38400,
              57600,
              115200,
              230400,
              250000,
              256000,
              512000,
              921600
            ],
            "markdownDescription": "That port's rate, in bits per second."
          },
          "nxwright.simulator.sdCard0": {
            "type": "string",
            "default": "",
            "markdownDescription": "A folder of the computer that stands for the screen's first SD card, `sd0/`, by its full path, when a simulation's launch configuration gives no `sdCard0`. `${workspaceFolder}` stands for the workspace's folder. Empty for none: the card is kept in memory."
          },
          "nxwright.simulator.sdCard1": {
            "type": "string",
            "default": "",
            "markdownDescription": "The same, for the second SD card, `sd1/`, and `sdCard1`."
          },
          "nxwright.simulator.pinyinTable": {
            "type": "string",
            "default": "",
            "markdownDescription": "The screen's pinyin table, for Chinese input, when a simulation's launch configuration gives no `pinyinTable`: the Nextion Editor's `input.bin`, or a TFT file, by its full path. `${workspaceFolder}` stands for the workspace's folder. Empty to use the installed Nextion Editor's, if one is found. Without a table, Chinese input shows no candidates."
          },
          "nxwright.simulator.logReceived": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "text",
              "hex",
              "both"
            ],
            "enumDescriptions": [
              "As text, read in the project's encoding; a byte that is no character shows as \\xNN.",
              "In hexadecimal, each byte as two digits.",
              "As text, then in hexadecimal."
            ],
            "default": "text",
            "markdownDescription": "How the simulator's log, in the Debug Console, shows what the screen receives on its serial line, when a simulation's launch configuration gives no `logReceived`."
          },
          "nxwright.simulator.logSent": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "text",
              "hex",
              "both"
            ],
            "enumDescriptions": [
              "As text, read in the project's encoding; a byte that is no character shows as \\xNN.",
              "In hexadecimal, each byte as two digits.",
              "As text, then in hexadecimal."
            ],
            "default": "hex",
            "markdownDescription": "How the simulator's log shows what the screen sends on its serial line, when a simulation's launch configuration gives no `logSent`. As text, the FF FF FF that ends a reply is left out."
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "title": "Agents",
        "properties": {
          "nxwright.agents.allowControl": {
            "type": "boolean",
            "default": false,
            "scope": "application",
            "markdownDescription": "Lets `nxwright mcp`, through which an AI agent drives your app, start and drive this window's simulator. Only a program that can read a file of your own account can connect. Only your user settings can turn it on, never a workspace's."
          },
          "nxwright.agents.startWithoutSerialPort": {
            "type": "boolean",
            "default": true,
            "scope": "application",
            "markdownDescription": "A simulation an agent starts has no serial port, whatever the Simulator settings say. Turned off, it takes the Simulator settings' port, and you are asked first if `#nxwright.agents.askBeforeSerialActions#` is on."
          },
          "nxwright.agents.askBeforeSerialActions": {
            "type": "boolean",
            "default": true,
            "scope": "application",
            "markdownDescription": "Asks you before an agent acts on a simulation whose serial port is connected, since what the app sends then reaches the device on that port. Your answer holds until the simulation ends."
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "title": "Tests",
        "properties": {
          "nxwright.testFolders": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "default": [],
            "markdownDescription": "The folders of tests that Test Explorer lists, relative to the workspace's first folder. When empty, each folder named `tests` beside a source folder."
          }
        }
      }
    ],
    "configurationDefaults": {
      "[nxwright]": {
        "files.encoding": "utf8",
        "files.autoGuessEncoding": false
      }
    },
